Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.75,0:00:02.20,Default,,0,0,0,,The Amazon rainforest is a
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.20,0:00:04.23,Default,,0,0,0,,type of tropical rainforest,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.23,0:00:05.77,Default,,0,0,0,,characterized by a closed and
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.77,0:00:07.74,Default,,0,0,0,,continuous tree canopy, with
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.74,0:00:09.72,Default,,0,0,0,,moisture-dependent vegetation,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.72,0:00:11.00,Default,,0,0,0,,and a diverse array of
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.00,0:00:12.85,Default,,0,0,0,,plant and animal species.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.55,0:00:14.53,Default,,0,0,0,,It has a warm and
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.53,0:00:16.67,Default,,0,0,0,,wet climate, with no substantial
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.67,0:00:18.26,Default,,0,0,0,,dry season, and plays a
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.26,0:00:19.89,Default,,0,0,0,,significant role in mitigating
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.89,0:00:21.16,Default,,0,0,0,,global warming.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.46,0:00:22.97,Default,,0,0,0,,The Amazon rainforest has seen
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.97,0:00:24.78,Default,,0,0,0,,a surge in fires, which
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.78,0:00:26.01,Default,,0,0,0,,can be devastating to the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.01,0:00:28.51,Default,,0,0,0,,ecosystem, with over 80,000
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.51,0:00:31.10,Default,,0,0,0,,fires reported in 2019, a
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.10,0:00:32.92,Default,,0,0,0,,77% increase from the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.92,0:00:34.14,Default,,0,0,0,,previous year.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.44,0:00:35.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Fires normally occur around the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.98,0:00:37.61,Default,,0,0,0,,dry season as slash-and-burn
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.61,0:00:38.80,Default,,0,0,0,,methods are used to clear
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.80,0:00:40.25,Default,,0,0,0,,the forest, leading to
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.25,0:00:42.80,Default,,0,0,0,,deforestation and habitat loss.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.10,0:00:44.08,Default,,0,0,0,,The fate of the Amazon
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.08,0:00:46.17,Default,,0,0,0,,rainforest is a concern, as
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.17,0:00:47.62,Default,,0,0,0,,it is estimated that over
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.62,0:00:50.16,Default,,0,0,0,,40% of all biotic species
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.16,0:00:51.11,Default,,0,0,0,,are indigenous to the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.11,0:00:52.89,Default,,0,0,0,,rainforests, and the loss of
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.89,0:00:54.88,Default,,0,0,0,,this ecosystem could have severe
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.88,0:00:55.79,Default,,0,0,0,,consequences for the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.79,0:00:56.70,Default,,0,0,0,,environment.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.00,0:00:58.59,Default,,0,0,0,,The Amazon rainforest is a
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.59,0:01:00.04,Default,,0,0,0,,moist broadleaf tropical
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.04,0:01:02.00,Default,,0,0,0,,rainforest, spanning over
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.00,0:01:04.86,Default,,0,0,0,,7 million km2, and is home to
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.86,0:01:07.36,Default,,0,0,0,,many species of plants, insects,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.36,0:01:09.63,Default,,0,0,0,,and microorganisms, making it a
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.63,0:01:10.76,Default,,0,0,0,,significant source of
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.76,0:01:12.04,Default,,0,0,0,,natural medicines.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.34,0:01:13.88,Default,,0,0,0,,The conservation of the Amazon
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.88,0:01:15.76,Default,,0,0,0,,rainforest is crucial, and
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.76,0:01:16.77,Default,,0,0,0,,efforts are being made to
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.77,0:01:18.93,Default,,0,0,0,,protect this vital ecosystem.